# A bare callable statement runs with its result discarded; the valued bare occurrence runs
# again and supplies 7. Explicit node\hits observes both calls without modifying a hidden input;
# the callee reads the graph path, not the caller's unchanged cached local value.
# The harness also requires two retained graph CALLs and the root's native trampoline.
int: hits 0
fn: ping () int
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
    return: node\hits + 5
end: ping

ping
int: r ping
if: r != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
